{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"BLOCKED — implementation not started. The plan's target code is not on origin/main.\n\nThe plan-review attestation is pinned to verified-at-sha c72b8e34ca8deab44b66bfbd2ec7617bf6f94a43. That SHA is NOT an ancestor of origin/main (1052bc856f). `git merge-base --is-ancestor c72b8e34ca HEAD` -> NO; merge-base is eeaa39e6e759cd204b001d15efad6363590a2442, with 28 commits on the c72b side. c72b8e34ca is reachable only from feat/5e75-adr0056, feat/7de4-rung-target and backup/pre-envgen-stack.\n\nConsequence: parent bug 03b0's fix has not landed. On origin/main, none of the plan's edit targets exist:\n- src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py — file absent (so _resolve_target absent)\n- tests/unit/test_provider_qualifier.py — absent\n- tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py — absent\n- split_provider_qualifier — absent (0 hits across src/ and tests/)\n- _PROVIDER_QUALIFIER_RE — absent\n- 'import re' in src/rebar/llm/config.py — absent (already not imported)\nAll three files DO exist at c72b8e34ca (git ls-tree confirms the blobs).\n\nWhat does exist on main sits at different lines than the plan cites: _PROVIDER_PREFIXES at config.py:322 (plan says 169), infer_provider at config.py:333 (plan says 213), ProviderSession._builders at providers.py:103 with the conditional openai at :115 (plan says 106/118), the unknown-provider raise at providers.py:173 (plan says 180). infer_provider on main still uses the raw `if \":\" in model` test at config.py:337 — i.e. the pre-03b0 shape, which is the defect 03b0 fixed.\n\n`rebar claim` correctly refused (exit 1, plan-review drift on all 4 dependency files) — this is a stale-base refusal, not a concurrency conflict; the ticket is still open with assignee null. Not force-claimed.\n\nTo unblock: either land 03b0 on main first, or re-base this story onto the branch carrying 03b0's fix and re-run review-plan there.\n\nSide finding (out of scope, confirmed by running the tree at origin/main): _PROVIDER_PREFIXES maps 'gemini' -> 'google_genai', and google_genai is in NEITHER runtime registry. infer_provider('gemini-2.5-pro') -> 'google_genai'; 'google_genai' in _pydantic_ai_known_providers() -> False; _builders is ['anthropic','bedrock'] (plus 'openai' only when base_url is set) -> False; ProviderSession.is_resolvable('google_genai') -> False; provider_factory('google_genai') raises LLMConfigError: unknown provider 'google_genai'; registered providers: ['anthropic', 'bedrock']. pydantic-ai knows google, google-cloud, google-gla, google-vertex, vertexai, gateway/google-cloud — but not google_genai. So any bare gemini-* id is unusable. CONFIRMED, and it reproduces on main independently of 03b0."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785687705996660001,"uuid":"86ee3201-38cc-4db2-8e64-0fef86e3e488"}